| `https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/` | `GET /?size=150x150&data=Hello` | Image File (MIME: image/png) |

| Category | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| Input Validation | Use `encodeURIComponent()` on `input.value` to ensure special characters (like &, ?, #) don't break the API query string. |
| Exception Handling | Wrap `fetch` calls in `try...catch` blocks to handle network timeouts or DNS failures gracefully. |
| UX Improvement | Use `input.value.trim()` to prevent generating QR codes for empty whitespace. |
| Logic Error | Verify `response.ok` before attempting to use the response, as `fetch` does not reject on 404 or 500 errors. |

Fixed code:
```js
const btn = document.getElementsByTagName('button')[0];
const imgbox = document.getElementById('imgBox');
const qrImage = document.getElementById('Qr-Image');
const input = document.getElementById('Qr-text');
const loadelement = document.createElement('p');

imgbox.append(loadelement);

/**
 * Fetches and displays a QR code based on user input.
 */
const getQR = async () => {
    const trimmedValue = input.value.trim();
    loadelement.hidden = false;
    loadelement.classList.remove('invalid-input');

    if (trimmedValue.length > 0) {
        try {
            qrImage.src = '';
            loadelement.innerHTML = 'Loading ...';

            // Use encodeURIComponent to handle special characters in input
            const apiUrl = `https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=150x150&data=${encodeURIComponent(trimmedValue)}`;

            const response = await fetch(apiUrl);

            if (!response.ok) {
                throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
            }

            // Setting src directly from response.url
            qrImage.src = response.url;
            loadelement.hidden = true;
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Error generating QR code:', error);
            qrImage.src = '';
            loadelement.classList.add('invalid-input');
            loadelement.innerHTML = 'Service Unavailable. Try again later.';
        }
    } else {
        qrImage.src = '';
        loadelement.classList.add('invalid-input');
        loadelement.innerHTML = 'Invalid Input !';
    }
};

btn.addEventListener('click', getQR);
```

